WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.575
Fire is the emergency every captain dreads.

2
00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:07.825
On the water there’s no fire department and nowhere to run.

3
00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:12.775
So today we learn how a fire works, because that tells you how to kill it.

4
00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:14.850
Look at the diagram.

5
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.150
A fire needs three things: heat, fuel and oxygen.

6
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.425
Plus a fourth, the chemical chain reaction that keeps it going.

7
00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:26.575
Take away any one, and the fire goes out.

8
00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:29.600
Cooling removes the heat.

9
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.300
Smothering removes the oxygen.

10
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.025
Shutting a valve removes the fuel.

11
00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:38.200
And dry chemical breaks the chain reaction.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.250
Fires are also sorted into classes by what’s burning.

13
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.375
Class A is ordinary stuff that leaves ash: wood, cushions, line.

14
00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:52.000
Class B is flammable liquids that boil: gasoline and oil.

15
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.650
That’s the most common boat fire.

16
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.200
Class C is energized electrical equipment, think current.

17
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.475
And Class D is combustible metals.

18
00:01:02.725 --> 00:01:05.700
A for ash, B for boil, C for current.
